<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL REAL ENDS OFF 0.05 PCT IN COMMERCIAL MARKET.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL REAL ENDS OFF 0.05 PCT IN COMMERCIAL MARKET.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's real ended off 0.05 percent at 1.0859 per dollar in the commercial foreign exchange market in calm trading Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the interbank floating rate market, the real closed down 0.04 percent at 1.0911 per greenback, while in the parallel market the real currency ended flat at 1.140 per dollar.</p>
<p>((-- Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485418))</p>
